# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit. Real values live in .env; .env.example holds names only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# The matplotlib font cache. CI points MPLCONFIGDIR here (see ci.yml) so the
# cache is built once rather than on every cold runner, which means the one
# artifact this project's own CI creates was the one artifact not ignored.
.mplcache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and agent scaffolding
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.envrc
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradio. The launch writes a certificate and a flagging directory next to the
# app, and the share tunnel binary is downloaded rather than vendored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradio/
flagged/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data. Rebuilt from the seed, never a source artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
question_queue.duckdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results.
#
# The rule is not "results are noise". Some of it is evidence and some of it is
# live output, and the difference decides whether the demo works.
#
# LIVE CELL OUTPUT IS IGNORED, and that is load-bearing. The sweep resumes from
# results/sweep/. A committed cell would arrive on every clone and make the FIRST
# live sweep on a fresh machine resume-and-complete instantly, rendering finished
# numbers to a room told nothing is precomputed. A test asserts a fresh clone
# renders "not yet measured".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/*.json
results/*.jsonl
# Derived, not evidence: build_gold memoises here, keyed on the warehouse seed plus a
# hash of gold/patterns.py and warehouse/semantic_model.yaml, so a rule edit invalidates
# it automatically. Committing it would ship an answer key nobody re-derived.
results/gold_cache.json
results/sweep/
results/ablation/
results/charts/
results/*.log
results/*.png
results/*.svg
results/_resume_marker*.txt

# Kept deliberately: the determinism floor the pre-registration cites BY NAME before
# the first cell runs. It was ignored, so the citation resolved to nothing on every
# clone — a provenance line pointing at a file that was not there. Committing the file
# was the fix; a test now asserts every repo path named in sweep/ resolves on disk.
!results/noise_floor_*.json

# Kept deliberately, AND FOR THE SAME REASON, one file later.
#
# `docs/the-failure-taxonomy.md` cites this by name as the record of which visible-
# failure kinds real runs have actually produced. It was written, committed with
# `git add -A`, and silently not added — because `results/*.json` above ignores it —
# so the local suite passed with the file sitting untracked on one machine and CI
# failed on the clone, exactly as the noise-floor citation once did.
#
# That is the noise-floor defect repeating with a different filename, and the thing
# that caught it was the clean checkout rather than the author's laptop.
!results/failure_taxonomy_observed.json

# Kept deliberately: the six arm summaries the experiments script writes. They are the
# only measurement in the repository that reaches LangSmith, and a comparison view that
# cannot be reproduced from disk is a comparison nobody can check.
!results/experiments/

# REMOVED, and the removals are recorded rather than deleted quietly: exceptions for
# `results/reference/`, `results/prefix_v1/`, `results/gate0.json`,
# `results/_resume_first.log` and `assets/` are gone because every one of those paths
# is gone. An un-ignore rule for a file that does not exist is harmless the day it is
# written and misleading afterwards — it reads as "this is committed on purpose", which
# is a claim about a file, and there is no file.

# There is no `assets/`. The committed README images, the tool that rendered them and
# the stored measurements it rendered from were all removed — every chart is drawn by
# the run that renders it now.
!assets/manifest.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staging and backups
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bundle
.hf-staging/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gold set is COMMITTED, under gold/. The memoised cache is not.
#
# The cache is a build artefact keyed on the warehouse seed plus a hash of the
# patterns and the semantic model, so a rule edit invalidates it automatically.
# `gold/gold.jsonl` is the contract: a reader opens it and sees the questions and
# the answers without running anything.
#
# That used to be refused, with the reasoning that committing it "would ship an
# answer key nobody re-derived". The objection was right and is now answered rather
# than ignored — scripts/validate_gold.py re-executes every query against a freshly
# seeded warehouse and fails on any drift, in CI, on every push.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!gold/
